/E (What is Digital-Smart Sprout? \(Digital Literacy\))
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
512 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 336 0 R
/E (A half-hour digital course to develop the habit  of keeping money safe where no scammer is even involved. It teaches the thing the online world is built to hide: money on a screen is real money, even a game's gems, even when a tap makes it vanish without a sound. So before you spend or share, pause and ask.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
513 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 336 0 R
/E (That gap, between how real the money is and how unreal it feels, is where children lose it. So before a child spends anything on a screen, they learn to pause and ask a grown-up. There's a quieter second idea running underneath: what you put online is real too, and it stays. A photo, a message, your name, where you live. Once it's out, it doesn't come back.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
