697 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 345 0 R
/E (A half-hour legal course that finishes the set. The other four taught a child to spot a bad deal, a fake, an invisible cost and a thief. By now the child can spot when something is wrong with money. This one answers the question they were all leading to: something's wrong, so what do I actually do? You're allowed to say no, you deserve a fair deal, and asking for help is your right.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
698 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 345 0 R
/E ( That's the whole of it. It does not teach law, courts or the Constitution. Those come much later, and even schools save them for the teenage years. Sprout Legal plants three usable instincts instead: say no, expect fair, get help. It is the piece that turns four courses of spotting trouble into knowing what to do)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
